ACTION: REVISE 6
TITLE: Hierarchical Facial Rigging for High-Complexity Meshes
PROPOSAL: Incorporate a self-supervised loss term to the hierarchical rigging pipeline that encourages the model to predict the same FACS parameters at each refinement stage, thus enforcing consistency across the hierarchical rigging process. This self-supervised regularizer should help to reduce the artifacts and inconsistencies that can arise from intermediate stage predictions.
CONTROLS: 
  - Keep Baseline - Single-stage facial auto-rigging;
  - Keep Ablation - No hierarchical refinement;
  - Keep Coarse rigging using pre-trained model;
  - Add Self-supervised loss term using FACS parameters.
COST: 8100 -> 10800
PREDICTION: The self-supervised loss term should significantly improve the rigging performance and consistency, but the trade-off between the increase in model capacity and the additional training complexity needs to be carefully balanced.
